  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef numpy_tile_diff(x: list, reps: int) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Tile and Diff** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef numpy_tile_diff(x: list, reps: int) -> list:\n    arr = np.array(x, dtype=np.float64)\n    tiled = np.tile(arr, (int(reps), 1))\n    diff = np.diff(tiled, axis=0)\n    diff_padded = np.vstack([np.zeros((1, tiled.shape[1]), dtype=np.float64), diff])\n    return np.stack([tiled, diff_padded], axis=0).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
